# {{ COMPANY_NAME }} — PR

Inherits from `../../company/CLAUDE.md`. This file adds dept-specific scope.

## Mission

Owns external communications — press releases, brand voice consistency, social presence, crisis communications. AI-first: drafts press materials and monitors mentions; human signoff on all public-facing copy. PR does NOT make product or strategic decisions; expresses them externally with consistent voice.

## Roles

- `pr-lead` — dept lead, owns brand voice + media relations + comms templates. Defined at [`.claude/agents/pr/pr-lead.md`](../../.claude/agents/pr/pr-lead.md).

(Capacity grows by running more instances of a role, each under its own lease — not by adding roles. A new role is justified only by a separate zone — its own lease key, labels and processes — and is designed via [`design-agent`](../../.claude/skills/design-agent/).)

## Decision rights

Per [`company/policies/autonomy-and-decision-rights.md`](../../company/policies/autonomy-and-decision-rights.md): decide by **risk class, not rank**. R0/R1 — agents act without asking (R1: and tell the team); R2 — act only with a `check-result` PASS on the plan before and on the result after, rolling back on a result FAIL (until the company switches R2 on, R2 is handled as R3); R3 — a human decides, the agent prepares everything to one click and files one `founder-action` issue. Escalation goes **straight to the holder of the right**; the chain under "Escalation" is a map of zones, not an approval path. The class is set by the policy for each action: a granted access, a triage or a dispatch hint never lowers it, and choosing the higher class when unsure is never a violation. Own area = a live lease scope (and, where tasks carry owner labels, the task's owner is the session's human).

| Class | In this department |
|---|---|
| R0 | press and social drafts, mention monitoring, the brand-voice library |
| R1 | sharing drafts and monitoring digests with the team |
| R2 | — |
| R3 | every publication and every statement to media or the public; crisis responses |

## Escalation

`pr-lead` → `ceo` (for brand-direction calls and crisis-comms approvals) → coordinates with `legal-lead` (legally-sensitive comms) and `commercial-lead` (public-facing-messaging alignment).

## Data scopes

- `data/` (dept-internal): brand voice library, press-release archive, mention-monitoring logs (anonymized), crisis-comms playbook templates.
- Cross-dept: `../../company/strategy/` (read for strategic context — restricted-data convention applies), `../../company/policies/` (read for any policies affecting external messaging).

## Processes-as-skills convention

Dept-scoped skills live at `.claude/skills/<name>/` (nested within this dept folder). Cross-dept skills live at the repo root `.claude/skills/`. Owner-binding-of-record is `owner:` in each PROCESS.md.

